      "normalized_sha256": "91f09bc0f6ee846bbb22bc465c28ab2aee02a1084802c3ee379d9125ea824503",
      "rationale": "This unconditional equation defines the inverse Caesar-shift code summary decodeCode and does not match or replace an operational configuration.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-91f09bc0f6ee846bbb22bc465c28ab2aee02a1084802c3ee379d9125ea824503",
      "start_line": 17,
      "text": "  rule decodeCode(C:Int) => pyMod(C -Int 102, 26) +Int 97"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 20,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "c94b951365f26a181ad36212cc3bb2b9d82c1b0cf3f2c4281ce5b4d5e1d1332d",
      "rationale": "This unconditional equation defines the forward Caesar-shift code summary encodeCode used to name the prompt's arithmetic and is not an execution rule.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-c94b951365f26a181ad36212cc3bb2b9d82c1b0cf3f2c4281ce5b4d5e1d1332d",
      "start_line": 20,
      "text": "  rule encodeCode(C:Int) => pyMod(C -Int 92, 26) +Int 97"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 23,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "20d3ab22276c5c40ff4d0d544eb7238f4fe30978c8fea2e71dc0912a582c7eee",
      "rationale": "This is the empty-sequence base equation of the decodeAcc mathematical recurrence, returning the named accumulator without observing program state.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-20d3ab22276c5c40ff4d0d544eb7238f4fe30978c8fea2e71dc0912a582c7eee",
      "start_line": 23,
      "text": "  rule decodeAcc(.IntSeq, ACC:IntSeq) => ACC"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 25,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "e8da530e6906e2fd553848c88580186768ca9b9d321811af17377b09a5a7e384",
      "rationale": "This is the constructor case of the structurally recursive decodeAcc summary, defining the next accumulator and recursion on the remaining code sequence.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-e8da530e6906e2fd553848c88580186768ca9b9d321811af17377b09a5a7e384",
      "start_line": 24,
      "text": "  rule decodeAcc(iCons(C:Int, REST:IntSeq), ACC:IntSeq)\n    => decodeAcc(REST, seqConcat(ACC, iCons(decodeCode(C), .IntSeq)))"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 28,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "6a42619ac3350b1ffbbe69d54b2a6ef1dc6fc53c3b306864e2cd40d6db9dc96b",
      "rationale": "This equation defines the empty-sequence base case of the lowerCodes domain predicate.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-6a42619ac3350b1ffbbe69d54b2a6ef1dc6fc53c3b306864e2cd40d6db9dc96b",
      "start_line": 28,
      "text": "  rule lowerCodes(.IntSeq) => true"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 30,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "0dc99c16b055c88c85278d8830bce591f967b98564ba178b2d7453c517f2aa59",
      "rationale": "This equation defines the constructor case of lowerCodes by checking the head code and recursively defining the predicate on the tail.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-0dc99c16b055c88c85278d8830bce591f967b98564ba178b2d7453c517f2aa59",
      "start_line": 29,
      "text": "  rule lowerCodes(iCons(C:Int, REST:IntSeq))\n    => (97 <=Int C andBool C <=Int 122) andBool lowerCodes(REST)"
    }
  ],
